  "priorExpiration": "2009-11-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5011.08 Inspection for Entry or Theft.\n\n(a) A magazine containing display fireworks shall be inspected at a minimum of every 7 days to determine whether there has been an unauthorized entry or attempted entry into the magazine or to determine whether there has been unauthorized removal of the magazine.\n\n(b) In addition to (a) above, a magazine containing display fireworks shall be opened at a minimum of every 7 days to determine whether there has been unauthorized removal of any of the contents of the magazine.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5000) #6055, eff 7-1-95; ss by #7481, eff 4-25-01, EXPIRED: 4-25-09\n\nNew. #9471, INTERIM, eff 5-15-09, EXPIRED: 11-11-09\n\nNew. #9765-A, eff 8-2-10; ss by #12738, eff 4-30-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5000.html"
